Z||000000||85blackgt||07-03-2001||12:15 PM||||i went to boot up my car this morning after changeing the fuel pump now it has been sitting for awile and im starting to do the tune ups now, but when i goto start it up it will almost catch, but i have to go and squirt gas into the injectors then she fires up any idea's?<P>------------------<BR>it's for the better your better half is gone. It's ok you didn't need her anyway. and i don't wanna  hear you say nobody can take her place and what more kan i say you didn't need her anyways.! -less than jake<P>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-03-2001||12:26 PM||||Does it only do this when the engine is cold? If it starts and runs fine when the engine is already warm, then it could be your cold-start injector or switch. If it does this at all times, it may be the fuel pump/oil pressure relay. Do you hear the fuel pump whine for a couple of seconds when you turn the key to on?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steven||07-03-2001||01:51 PM||||It sound to me like your fuel pump is not kicking on to prime the system. Turn the ign to on, listen to the fuel pump. Did it kick on? If it kicked on, check to see what the fuel pressure is. Service manual will tell you what the correct pressure should be, I don't know it off the top of my head. Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||07-03-2001||03:47 PM||||Fuel pressure should be 41-47 psi.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steven||07-03-2001||04:17 PM||||Thanks, I knew someone would know it off the top of their head.||||reg||1
